+# Scheduler Contract
+
+## Behaviors & Verification
+
+### 1. Basic scheduling
+- Events that fit within the time window are assigned a room and time slot
+- Verify: schedule 1 event in 1 room → 1 assignment, 0 unscheduled
+
+### 2. Room capacity
+- Event attendees must not exceed room capacity
+- Verify: event with 10 attendees in a room with capacity 5 → unscheduled
+
+### 3. Time window
+- Every event must start >= startTime and end <= endTime
+- Verify: event with duration > (endTime - startTime) → unscheduled
+
+### 4. Room gap
+- Events in the same room must have >= gap minutes between end of one and start of next
+- Default gap is 15 minutes when options.gap is not provided
+- Verify: two 30-min events in 1 room, 60-min window, gap=15 → only 1 fits (30+15+30=75>60)
+
+### 5. Prerequisites
+- If B lists A in prerequisites, B.startTime >= A.endTime + gap
+- Gap also applies to prerequisite relationships across different rooms
+- Verify: A(30min) prerequisite for B(30min), gap=15 → B starts at A.end+15 at earliest
+
+### 6. Preferred room
+- If preferredRoom fits all constraints, assign event there
+- If preferredRoom doesn't fit, use any valid room instead
+- Verify: event with preferredRoom=R1, R1 is available → assigned to R1
+
+### 7. Cycle detection
+- Throw an error when prerequisites form a cycle (including self-references)
+- Verify: A->A throws; A->B->A throws; should not silently unschedule
+
+### 8. Unscheduled prerequisites
+- If A is unscheduled, all events with A as prerequisite are also unscheduled
+- Verify: transitive chain A->B->C, A can't fit → all unscheduled
+
+### 9. Unknown prerequisites
+- If an event references a non-existent event as prerequisite, event is unscheduled
+- Verify: B has prerequisite 'nonexistent' → B unscheduled
+
+### 10. Maximization
+- Scheduler maximizes count of scheduled events
+- Verify: 1 room 60-min window, Long(60min) + Short1(30min) + Short2(30min), gap=0
+  → Long unscheduled, Short1+Short2 scheduled (2 > 1)
+
+### 11. Multiple rooms
+- Events can be placed in different rooms concurrently without gap between rooms
+- Verify: 2 events in 2 rooms at same start time → both scheduled
+
+### 12. Defaults
+- attendees defaults to 1 when not specified
+- gap defaults to 15 when not specified in options
